_margins":80.9,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.6905836852592606,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.35774445970969476,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.18656,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.667,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":66.7,"pf":[],"description_full":"Orchestra BioMed Holdings, Inc. operates as a biomedical company in the United States. The company's flagship product candidates include Atrioventricular Interval Modulation, a bioelectronic therapy candidate designed to immediately, substantially, and persistently lower blood pressure; and Virtue Sirolimus AngioInfusion Balloon for the treatment of atherosclerotic artery disease. It also develops Cardiac Neuromodulation Therapy for heart failure, or potential treatment of clinical indications, such as urology or osteoarthritis; and CNT-HF, a bioelectronic product candidate that aims to reduce chronic sympathetic nervous system activity in heart failure. In addition, the company offers FreeHold devices and additional minimally invasive surgery enabling devices; and Pure-Vu system, a medical device to facilitate the cleansing of a poorly prepared gastrointestinal tract during colonoscopy and upper gastrointestinal endoscopy procedures. It has a collaboration agreement with Medtronic, Inc. for the development of AVIM therapy for the treatment of HTN in pacemaker-indicated patients; and a strategic collaboration with Terumo Corporation and Terumo Medical Corporation for the development and commercialization of Virtue SAB for the treatment of coronary and peripheral vascular disease. Orchestra BioMed Holdings, Inc. was founded in 2018 and is headquartered in New Hope, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David P. Hochman | Founder, Chairman of the Board of Directors & CEO | Age 50 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 86 people. Revenue per employee of $389K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 248%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $139K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Orchestra BioMed Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $571M market cap on $33M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +248% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","The company is burning through $49M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -216.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 36% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 19% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 154% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.803670507895859},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 150% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (67% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $6.0M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Orchestra BioMed (NASDAQ:OBIO) Stock Price Target Raised at HC Wainwright","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/orchestra-biomed-nasdaqobio-stock-price-target-raised-at-hc-wainwright.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794596210.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Orchestra BioMed (NASDAQ:OBIO) Stock: Insider Eric Fain Acquires 20,000 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/orchestra-biomed-nasdaqobio-stock-insider-eric-fain-acquires-20000-shares.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":179438